"ly.eyebrow":"Focus Programme","ly.h2":"Lymphedema Treatment: Early Surgery Makes a Difference",
"ly.lead":"Lymphedema is not a fate to be managed with bandaging and massage alone for years. It is a condition that can be treated microsurgically from its early stages. Correct staging determines the correct method.",
"ly.m1.h":"Lymphaticovenous Anastomosis","ly.m1.p":"Connecting blocked lymphatic channels to small veins roughly 0.3–0.8 mm wide under the microscope. The least invasive option in early-stage disease, usually performed through small incisions.",
"ly.m2.h":"Vascularised Lymph Node Transfer","ly.m2.p":"Transferring lymph nodes with their blood supply from a healthy donor site to the affected region. Preferred in advanced stages and where lymphatic channel damage is widespread.",
"ly.m3.h":"Debulking Surgery and Liposuction","ly.m3.p":"Reducing volume and pain using lymphatic-sparing liposuction techniques. The primary treatment in lipedema and a complementary step in advanced lymphedema.",
"ly.m4.h":"Arm Lymphedema After Breast Cancer","ly.m4.p":"Combined approaches for arm swelling following axillary node dissection and radiotherapy, which can be planned alongside breast reconstruction.",
"ly.c.h":"Is your swelling lymphedema or lipedema?","ly.c.l":"Lymphedema","ly.c.r":"Lipedema",
"ly.c.1l":"Usually asymmetric — one side markedly worse","ly.c.1r":"Typically symmetric — both sides similar",
"ly.c.2l":"Swelling extends to the top of the foot and toes","ly.c.2r":"Swelling stops at the ankle; feet are spared",
"ly.c.3l":"Skin feels tight; may pit on pressure","ly.c.3r":"Tissue is soft; often painful to touch",
"ly.c.4l":"Diet and weight loss do not resolve the swelling","ly.c.4r":"Fat deposits resistant to weight loss",
"ly.c.note":"This table is for general information only and does not replace a clinical examination. Not every leg swelling is oedema; definitive diagnosis requires medical assessment and, where indicated, lymphoscintigraphy or ICG lymphography.",
"ly.c.cta":"Send your images via WhatsApp","ly.c.more":"Full guide: staging, diagnosis and surgical methods →",
"pr.eyebrow":"The Process","pr.h2":"From first message to final check-up","pr.lead":"A transparent, unhurried roadmap where every step is known in advance.",
"pr.1h":"Initial contact","pr.1p":"First contact by WhatsApp or phone. Initial guidance is given based on your complaint, previous treatments and any images you share.",
"pr.2h":"Examination and planning","pr.2p":"A detailed in-person or online assessment. Required imaging, applicable methods, risks and realistic expectations are discussed openly.",
"pr.3h":"Surgery","pr.3p":"Performed in a fully equipped hospital setting, with a multidisciplinary team where required. Anaesthesia and hospital stay are clarified beforehand.",
"pr.4h":"Recovery and follow-up","pr.4p":"Scheduled check-ups, wound care and physiotherapy referral where needed. Online follow-up for out-of-town and international patients.",
"ab.eyebrow":"Your Surgeon","ab.h2":"Assoc. Prof. Dr. Tahsin Oğuz Acartürk",
"ab.p1":"After graduating from Hacettepe University School of Medicine, he completed his specialty training in the United States. He is the first Turkish plastic surgeon accepted into the University of Pittsburgh's integrated plastic surgery programme.",
"ab.p2":"He served as Director of Head and Neck Reconstruction at the University of Pittsburgh. To date he has performed over 600 microsurgical operations. He is among the first Turkish plastic surgeons to work on stem cells, tissue engineering and adipose tissue technologies.",
"ab.p3":"He received the European Association of Plastic Surgeons' \"Young Plastic Surgeon\" award, worked as a fellow at the University of Helsinki, and holds an Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery subspecialty from the Turkish Ministry of Health. Each year he joins volunteer surgical missions in Vietnam, performing microtia, cleft lip and palate, and brachial plexus surgery.",
"ab.q":"\"Giving back what nature gave is hard. A good surgeon never treats a case as simple.\"","ab.qc":"Assoc. Prof. Dr. Tahsin Oğuz Acartürk",
"ab.t1b":"HACETTEPE UNIVERSITY","ab.t1s":"<strong>Doctor of Medicine</strong> — School of Medicine",
